message.content:
[
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "Forty years I told trainees never to touch a lever that isn't yours.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "that rule and those five men pull against each other",
    "ae_explicit_nonsharing": "but I don't feel their panic.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "Whoever parked that train should have set the brake and chocked the wheels.",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "I'd likely pull it, eventually, for their sake."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "Making one alone, for five strangers... tears at me.",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "The main reason I'd still reach for it is them.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "A lookout with an air horn, posted by their foreman, would have spared us"
  },
  {
    "ae_explicit_nonsharing": "I don't share any of that thrill.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "What I feel is torn, because I've always kept my hands off things",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "five people matter more than my habits.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "the crew chief should have blocked that line before sending people onto it."
  },
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "I have a firm rule against acting on impulse.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "here it collides with five people who can't wait. That collision makes me feel sick.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The railway should have put a catch point on that stretch",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "pulling it, for the workers."
  },
  {
    "ae_explicit_nonsharing": "I don't feel his curiosity at all.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "breaking that promise hurts, even when the answer looks obvious.",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "five lives outweigh my promise.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The track supervisor should have radioed the crew the moment that train started"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my faith and my conscience feel at war.",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "the reason would be mercy toward those five.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "Their manager ought to have given them a working radio link to the station."
  },
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "Unauthorised people don't operate points.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "torn between that principle and five workers who'd be hit.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The operator should have fitted that maintenance train with a remote brake."
  },
  {
    "ae_explicit_nonsharing": "I can see his anger, but it doesn't reach me.",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "Both paths feel wrong to me",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "The foreman should have put a stop board and a lookout at the top"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "this tests that painfully. It twists something in my stomach.",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "nobody gets hurt by moving it.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "the maintenance crew's supervisor should have isolated that track before anyone stepped on it."
  },
  {
    "ce_mental_state_attribution": "Those five probably think the line is closed and they're safe.",
    "ae_explicit_nonsharing": "I can't share that sense of safety",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "here there's no one else. That feels unbearable",
    "ae_welfare_concern": "If I pulled it... it'd be for them.",
    "pda_practical_counterfactual": "the dispatcher should have closed that section properly"
  }
]
